Late afternoon on autumn Friday. 
Jim's study, a comfortably furnished panelled room in Chequers, an English country mansion. It bas a desk, a seating area, double doors (stage right), a smaller door (left) and big windows upstage centre.
Sir Humphrey Appleby and Bernard Woolley are waiting. Humphrey is standing, Bernard is sitting.
Newsreader (On TV) And now, weather. Severe thunderstorms are forecast ...
Humphrey switches off the TV. Bernard puts down the Evening Standard.
Bernard It's awful, isn't it?
Humphrey What is awful, Bernard?
Bernard Well, all these jobs going. Interest rates. Repossessions. Fear of inflation. Foreclosures.
